NAME
     shutdown - stop the machine

SYNOPSIS
     shutdown [-h|-r|-H] [-f] [now|+MINUTES|hh:mm] [MESSAGE]
     halt     reboot     poweroff

DESCRIPTION
     shutdown warns everyone logged in, waits, and then stops the
     machine: init runs the stop scripts, processes are asked and then
     told to go, file systems are written out and unmounted, and the
     machine halts, reboots or powers off. halt, reboot and poweroff are
     the same program with the answer already chosen.

OPTIONS
     -h   halt
     -r   reboot
     -H   halt without powering off
     -f   skip the file system check on the way up

SEE ALSO
     init(8), telinit(8), sync(1)
